  "description": "Construction of shed in garden for additional space as partner is pregnant. It follows PD rules, but we didn't realise that we don't have class E PD as the house was split into flats in the past, despite us owning the whole garden front and back, and ground floor. \n\n2.5m high from highest ground level adjacent as within 2m of boundary. Slopes down towards boundary. Covers less than 50% of curtilage. Sited in the rear garden, behind the principal elevation. Use is incidental to the enjoyment of the main dwelling. \n\nIt is to be clad in dark green painted timber and is set below the level of mature vegetation. No trees are affected by the works. There is no impact on other people living in the flat as they do no have access to the garden and the highest point is below their lowest window level. It is not visible from the street. It is not visible directly from the rear due to mature planting. It is lower than a permitted fence at the boundary.\n\nThere is no plumbing. Rain is captured in water butts and used to water the garden. ",
